<section class="principles section-wrap" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="section-kicker">THE AUTHORING MODEL</p>
    <h2 id="principles-title">Keep application logic ordinary.</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="principle-grid">
    <article class="principle">
      <span class="principle-index">01</span>
      <h3>Write Odin you recognize</h3>
      <p>Layout and controls are functions in your render procedure. Application data stays in your structs and procedures.</p>
      <a href="/docs/getting-started/first-app">See a small app <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>
    <article class="principle">
      <span class="principle-index">02</span>
      <h3>Retain what should persist</h3>
      <p>Stable identity lets focus, selection, scroll, geometry, and shaped text survive a new description.</p>
      <a href="/docs/concepts/retained-runtime">Understand retention <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>
    <article class="principle">
      <span class="principle-index">03</span>
      <h3>Do work when it is dirty</h3>
      <p>Invalidation is explicit. The runtime reuses unchanged products and schedules only the dependent work a change requires.</p>
      <a href="/docs/concepts/invalidation">Follow a change <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
